@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container animate-fade-in-up" style="max-width: 800px; margin-top: 50px;">
    <div class="glass-card p-5">
        <h2 class="fw-bold text-white mb-4"><i class="bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-primary me-2"></i>Privacy Policy & Data Security</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">Effective Date: August 18, 2026</p>
        
        <p class="text-secondary mt-4">
            At <strong>Antigravity Gear & Travel E-Store</strong> (designed by Team 5: Bashar, Shorouq, Dawood), we are committed to protecting the privacy and security of our adventure community. This policy outlines how we gather, protect, and use your personal information.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-white fw-bold mt-4">1. Information We Collect</h4>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            To provide you with a premium shopping experience, we collect billing and shipping details (such as full name, email address, phone number, and physical address) during the checkout process. Account creation also saves your email and encrypted security credentials.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-white fw-bold mt-4">2. Secure Payment Processing</h4>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            Payment details (such as credit card numbers, expiration dates, and CVVs) are processed exclusively using simulated secure API integrations. We do not store credit card credentials on our servers.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-white fw-bold mt-4">3. Cart & Wishlist Persistence</h4>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            To allow shopping without log in, we utilize secure browser sessions and essential cookies. These cookies maintain your shopping cart selections until you log in to pay or clear your browsing data.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-white fw-bold mt-4">4. Customer Reviews & Testimonials</h4>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            When you submit comments, ratings, or stories, they are uploaded to our database and displayed publicly after approval by the Administrator. We do not display private user credentials alongside public comments.
        </p>

        <div class="border-top border-secondary pt-4 mt-5">
            <a asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-camping-primary">
                <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i>Return to Home
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
